              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Forwarded-header spoofing can partition public rate-limit identity\n\ngetClientIp trusts the first X-Forwarded-For token without a trusted-proxy boundary.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Input validation\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-345\n\nRemediation:\nUse an authenticated edge client-IP source.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Negative case fails closed and valid path remains functional.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant at the database, transaction, or trusted edge boundary."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
