                  "startLine": 21
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Direct Share-session writes bypass readiness and recipient governance\n\nOwner writes can construct recipients, access policy, status, and expiry without readiness checks.\n\nSeverity: low\n\nCategory: Improper authorization\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-863\n\nRemediation:\nCreate sessions only through a trusted transactional function.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Negative case fails closed and valid path remains functional.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant at the database, transaction, or trusted edge boundary."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c72473d41ff8bddd89ac99b8bba2f22f35a3a761d7e70ade0ab2c7d979644aa7"
          },
